{title: Pride}
{lyricist: Sergio Rykov}
{composer: Sergio Rykov}

{start_of_verse}
To know is not to be able,
To speak is not to do.
When boredom strikes my day,
Then pride walks into my home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
The joy of the day shatters to pieces,
Vanishing in the bustle of news.
Behind the false creaks of speed
Only the shadow of days remains.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
What's the time?
Seconds, minutes, hours.
Day after day they soon go by,
Turning into bubbles of years,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
They close the ring of old age.
And they see no way out of it.
In my head the heavy, echoing steps
Of pity are thundering.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Echoing with falseness,
Nasty things tear us apart.
Whoever knows what comes next
Will turn onto the course of clarity.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
There will be no special moral here,
Everyone is the captain of their ship.
And the clearer the distances seem,
Here's the question - and where am I here?
{end_of_verse}
